  "label": "User projected onto the absurd juxtaposition of cats and bacon",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the overall scene (bacon_and_cats_scene) which is framed as an arbitrary, nonsensical pairing by the text 'for no reason'. The humor arises from the user being invited to perceive the image as a random, absurd combination, without any logical connection, which is a common meme format. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but the phrase 'for no reason' implicitly invites the user to accept the absurdity as the point of the meme.",
